    feat: enforced argument-size maximum + committed arg-size benchmark. Addresses TJ-GAP-086.
    
    Policy (option a): intercept() refuses any command whose UTF-8 size exceeds
    TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_MAX_ARG_BYTES (default 262144 = 256 KiB) with a
    clean BLOCK naming the knob and the limit, checked BEFORE parsing so an
    oversize input costs O(len), never the linear engine scan. Under the limit
    verdict behavior is byte-identical (pinned). Warn mode degrades the refusal
    to allow-with-warning; disabled mode passes through. Unset/invalid/zero knob
    values fall back to the default (fail-safe).
    
    Benchmark: scripts/arg_size_benchmark.py — committed, bounded, laptop
    seconds; in-process intercept(), builtins-only via the quickstart 3a2
    empty-rules-dirs pinning; small / 8 KB / 20 KB cells, table output,
    optional --ceiling-check.
    
    Ceiling: tests/test_arg_size_ceiling.py runs the benchmark's measure_cell
    and fails above 20x the documented measurements (headroom stated in the
    test docstring; jitter-proof by design).
    
    Docs: README "Environment variables and limits" subsection; docs/quickstart.md
    3a2 retires the stale no-length-bound paragraph (TJ-DF-024's latency half was
    the prefilter fix; the bound half is this gate); CHANGELOG entry.
    
    Regression guards hold: TJ-DF-024 suite (soundness at 8 KB, 200 KB benign
    fixture, no length-based skip vocabulary) unmodified and green; full plugin
    + tests scope green (1787 + 123 passed, skips pre-existing).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
    
